\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


A positive cooriented contact structure on an oriented closed $3$-manifold $Y$ is $\xi=\ker\alpha$, with $\alpha\wedge d\alpha>0$. It is tight if it has no overtwisted disk. A symplectic cobordism from $(Y_-,\xi_-)$ to $(Y_+,\xi_+)$ is a compact symplectic $4$-manifold with boundary $-Y_-\sqcup Y_+$. It is exact when $\omega=d\lambda$ and the Liouville vector field defined by $\iota_V\omega=\lambda$ points inward at $Y_-$, outward at $Y_+$, and induces the specified contact structures. A weak symplectic cobordism satisfies positivity of $\omega|_{\xi_\pm}$ on the oriented contact planes. A weak filling is connected, has only the positive boundary and that positivity condition.
The support genus $\operatorname{sg}(Y,\xi)$ is the minimum page genus among open books supporting $\xi$. An open book supports $\xi$ when some contact form is positive on its oriented binding and its differential is positive on page interiors. The Giroux torsion $\operatorname{GT}(Y,\xi)$ is the supremum of integers $n\ge1$ for which
\[
\bigl(T^2\times[0,1],\ker(\cos(2\pi nt)\,dx+\sin(2\pi nt)\,dy)\bigr)
\]
contact-embeds in $(Y,\xi)$, with value $0$ if none and $\infty$ if unbounded. Legendrian surgery is contact $(-1)$ surgery on a knot tangent to $\xi$, with framing one less than the contact framing.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Determine how contact properties change under symplectic cobordisms, in particular:
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $\xi_-$ is tight and an exact symplectic cobordism runs from $(Y_-,\xi_-)$ to $(Y_+,\xi_+)$, must $\xi_+$ be tight?
\item If $\xi_-$ is weakly fillable and there is a weak symplectic cobordism to $(Y_+,\xi_+)$, must $\xi_+$ be weakly fillable?
\item Determine the changes in support genus and Giroux torsion under Legendrian surgery; in particular, must support genus be nondecreasing and Giroux torsion nonincreasing?
\end{enumerate}
\href{https://math.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/surv-295-ruberman-watermarked-author-pdf.pdf}{[S2]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
Does exact symplectic cobordism preserve tightness, does weak cobordism preserve weak fillability, and how does Legendrian surgery change support genus and Giroux torsion?

